   "he": "וּמְקָרְדִין אֶת הַבְּהֵמָה בְּיוֹם טוֹב. תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: אֵיזֶהוּ קֵרוּד וְאֵיזֶהוּ קִרְצוּף? קֵרוּד — קְטַנִּים וְעוֹשִׂין חַבּוּרָה, קִרְצוּף — גְּדוֹלִים וְאֵין עוֹשִׂין חַבּוּרָה.",
   "en": "§ It is taught in the mishna that Rabbi Elazar ben Azarya holds that «one may comb an animal on a Festival. The Sages taught» in a baraita: «What is» considered «combing and what is brushing? Combing» is performed with «a small»-toothed comb «and makes a wound; brushing» is done with «a large»-toothed comb «and does not make a wound.»"
  }
